      "content": "Here's a revised draft:\n\n\"Dear [Boss's Name],\n\nI wanted to touch base with you about the feature rollout for our cloud platform. Unfortunately, the scope has been creeping up on us, with new requirements emerging unexpectedly. It's like a stealthy band of mischievous goblins, sneaking in under the radar and making it impossible for us to stick to our original plan.\n\nAs a result, I'm concerned that we're at risk of compromising quality or, worse, delaying the launch. To mitigate this risk, I'd like to propose two options: either we bring in additional engineers to help manage the increased complexity, or we push back the launch date by two weeks to give ourselves more time to refine the scope.\n\nI believe either of these options would be a more sustainable approach, allowing us to deliver a high-quality feature that meets our customers' expectations.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\"\n\nI've tried to make it more concise and direct, while also emphasizing the idea of the scope creeping up on you like a sneaky band of goblins.",
